node_modules
# `dist` is TRACKED as of 2026-08-27, and it is a deliberate exception.
#
# The Databricks workspace folder is a GIT FOLDER (Arjun's call: the workspace
# must reflect pushes to GitHub, not local `databricks sync` runs). Databricks
# Git folders have NO BUILD STEP — they check out exactly what is committed —
# and review_app_react/backend/app.py serves `frontend/dist`. So a branch
# without a built dist deploys an app that serves nothing.
#
# THE COST, and it is real: `npm run build` must be run BEFORE committing any
# UI change, or the workspace gets a stale frontend with no error to warn you.
# `npm run build` is idempotent, so when in doubt, run it and commit.
dist-ssr
